            <ArticleTitle>Recent advances in paediatric respiratory medicine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>193-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/archdischild-2014-307212</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review highlights important advances in paediatric respiratory medicine since 2014, excluding cystic fibrosis. It focuses mainly on the more common conditions, bronchopulmonary dysplasia, bronchiolitis and preschool wheezing, asthma, pneumonia and sleep, and highlights some of the rarer conditions such as primary ciliary dyskinesia and interstitial lung disease (ILD).</AbstractText>
